KNOWNBUG (header-free, cvise-reduced-then-repaired isolation of
cpp17_tuple_basic).  Mirrors libstdc++ std::tuple: a variadic converting
constructor guarded by a defaulted SFINAE template parameter whose condition is a
TWO-parallel-pack fold over the class pack and the constructor's own pack
(`_TupleConstraints<_Elements...>::ic<_UElements...>()` ==
`and_<is_ctible<_Elements,_UElements>::value...>::value`).  For THREE elements
CBMC fails to evaluate that constraint, reports "found no match for symbol
'tuple'" during make_tuple's construction, so the tuple is unconstructed and
get<0> reads a nondeterministic value (get<0> == 1 fails).  Two elements are
handled correctly, and a plain (unconstrained) variadic constructor is handled
correctly, so the residual is the two-parallel-pack constexpr constraint in a
variadic constructor's SFINAE default template argument at >= 3 elements.  Both
g++ and clang++ accept and run the program with get<0> == 1.  Flip to CORE once
that constraint is evaluated at >= 3 elements.
